<MarketingLayout title="Guides — Frostdev" description="Practical guides to building a Rimeward workspace, connecting two computers with Crosspane, and coordinating agents with Rimewire." path="/guides">
  <div class="product-page reading-page">
    <p class="product-eyebrow">Frostdev guides</p>
    <h1>Put the tools to work.</h1>
    <p>Start with a specific task. Each guide explains the setup, the choices that matter, and a way to check the result. These guides are written from our projects' documentation; follow the linked release notes when your installed version differs.</p>

    <h2><a href="/guides/rimeward-first-workspace">Build your first Rimeward project workspace</a></h2>
    <p>Open a local folder, connect the Editor, Terminal and Rime to it, and finish with a small change you can review. Learn which tools need a provider and how to keep your project on its owning computer.</p>

    <h2><a href="/guides/crosspane-two-computers">Connect a Mac and Linux desk with Crosspane</a></h2>
    <p>Pair two computers, choose their permissions, and arrange the display edges. Check input control before trying window projection, and know how to take control back.</p>

    <h2><a href="/guides/rimewire-agent-handoffs">Make agent handoffs useful with Rimewire</a></h2>
    <p>Turn a project tracker into a shared board. Give work packages clear completion criteria and leave progress, blocker and review updates that another agent can use.</p>

    <h2>Need a different starting point?</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/#projects">project hub</a> links to the products, source repositories and installation documentation. If a guide is unclear or out of date, <a href="mailto:admin@frostdev.io">tell us which step needs attention</a>.</p>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>
